## VERIFIED CLEAN (with how I confirmed)

- **Panic-boundary completeness — TOTAL on both rows.** napi: EVERY method in `impl Session`
  carries `#[napi(.., catch_unwind)]` AND wraps its body in `guarded(env, "<name>", || …)`
  — enumerated the full attribute list from the anchor map (constructor 5561; addSheet 5572;
  setValue 5592; setFormula 5618; clear 5641; recalcDirty 5654; recalcAll 5667;
  startRecalcDirty 5687; startRecalcAll 5702; awaitRecalc 5720; cancel 5749; operationStatus
  5783; snapshot 5808; cell 5821; listSheets 5841; lifecycleState 5875; validateFormula 5886;
  queryRange 5911; markVolatilesDirty 5936; setFormat 5950; registerFormat 5972; close 5996;
  open 6020; import 6041; save 6055; export 6070; renameSheet 6099; deleteSheet 6113;
  restoreSheet 6127; moveSheet 6143; setName 6171; createTable 6203; renameTable 6219;
  renameColumn 6234; resizeTable 6255; dropTable 6279; batch 6314; beginTransaction 6344;
  txnAdd 6359; commitTransaction 6377; rollbackTransaction 6396; writeRange 6420;
  publishDataset 6444; bindRange 6465; refreshSource 6479; materializeQuery 6503;
  registerFunction 6562; unregisterFunction 6609; listFunctions 6629; setUdfWorker 6666;
  pollEvents 6735; snapshotDelta 6778; undo 6795; redo 6809; canUndo 6822; canRedo 6829).
  `__forcePanicForTest` (6855) is `#[cfg(debug_assertions)]`-gated, in a SECOND
  `impl Session` block (6854), debug-only, documented. pyo3: every method in
  `#[pymethods] impl Session` (src/lib.rs:788-1075) wraps in `guarded(py, "<name>", || …)`;
  probe at src/lib.rs:1069. `guarded` on both = catch_unwind → `EngineError::panic` → code
  `"panic"` (napi lib.rs:4330-4341 / pyo3 src/lib.rs:138-146); release-build caveat handled
  symmetrically by both emitters (`note:"probe-absent-release"`).
- **Error taxonomy cannot fork for engine-taxonomy errors.** Both bindings route every
  engine error through a converter that READS `e.code`/`e.class`/`e.retryable` from the SAME
  engine `EngineError` (napi throw_structured lib.rs:4275-4293 sets .code/.class/.retryable/
  .details(JSON-string)/.source; pyo3 engine_error_to_pyerr src/lib.rs:93-124 sets the
  identical five attributes). Neither maps variants→codes itself — codes are produced once
  in the engine (map_runtime_err/map_oplog_err/map_function_registry_err, exhaustive per
  §5.4 + Appendix A). `class_str` byte-identical (napi lib.rs:4297-4310 vs pyo3
  src/lib.rs:74-87). The matrix masks ONLY `version`/`nextCursor` (parity_matrix.py:41);
  error `code`s compared verbatim.
- **FFI `bad_argument` channel parity.** napi `bad_argument_error` (lib.rs:564) produces the
  `[bad_argument]`-prefix string with default `.code`; the `.mjs` errCode recovers it from
  the prefix; pyo3 `bad_argument` (src/lib.rs:129) sets a NATIVE `.code="bad_argument"` and
  the `.py` _err_code reads it. For the codes the golden flow exercises (err_bad_kind →
  unknown value kind; err_dup_sheet → sheet_name_duplicate; err_register_builtin →
  function_exists; err_post_close → invalid_state) both rows converge — the matrix passing
  proves it.
- **engine_error_to_napi degrades RICHNESS only, never masks (No-Fallbacks).** On a
  structured-throw build failure (lib.rs:4263-4265) it STILL surfaces `e` via `{e}` Display
  AND appends the build failure so the binding defect is visible — not a swallow. throw_structured
  surfaces a details-serialize failure loud (lib.rs:4283-4285). pyo3 mirror surfaces setattr
  failure (src/lib.rs:120-123) + details-serialize as a panic error (:107-112).
- **No-Fallbacks discipline in input converters.** napi session_cell_value_from_json,
  session_format_id_from_json (lib.rs:4492-4551), session_op_from_json (:4604-4663),
  session_table_spec_from_json (:4579), arity_from_json and the pyo3 twins are STRICT tagged
  unions: `reject_extra` on every off-kind field, loud `bad_argument` on missing required
  fields and unknown kinds, non-finite numbers rejected. No `|| default`, no swallowed
  errors. The §3.5 reserved stubs validate inputs to keep types honest but always return
  `not_implemented_in_v1_core` (documented they deliberately do NOT enforce the full input
  contract — that lands with the real impl).
- **Numeric boundary validators equivalent; no silent ToUint32.** napi validate_u32_index/
  validate_u16_index (lib.rs:175/225) reject non-finite/negative/fractional/oversize; all
  `WorkbookSession` coord/dim args are `f64` so they reach the validator UN-coerced
  (addSheet chunk_rows: f64 5573; setValue/cell coords f64; createTable via
  session_table_spec_from_json; format payloads `Option<f64>` via session_format_id_from_json).
  Found NO get_uint32/ToNumber coercion in any 6.3 Session method. BigInt→u64 rejects
  sign+non-lossless (transaction_id_from_bigint lib.rs:4674; customPeer :4528-4538). pyo3
  validate_u32_index/validate_u16_index (src/lib.rs:168/196) + u64_from_pyany (:766) impose
  the same domain. (NOTE: the u64 OUTPUT representation is HIGH-1/HIGH-2; INPUT validation is
  clean.)
- **Parity comparator is non-vacuous.** parity_matrix.py: run_emitter refuses a transcript
  that isn't a list of ≥10 records (:74-76); success branch is literal `node_t == py_t` deep
  equality on the FULLY-MASKED structures (:97), with a first-divergence diff (:80-87).
  Masking is NARROW (named keys only, recursive, :44-56) so it cannot blank a sibling key.
  `if __name__ == "__main__": raise SystemExit(main())` (:111-112) — exit code IS propagated
  (main returns 1 on mismatch). The ≥10 guard is sound (the flow emits ~27 step records).
- **Both rows run the SAME steps.** golden_flow.mjs:84-231 vs golden_flow.py:107-251 read
  side by side: identical step sequence + names (lifecycle_initial, add_sheet, recalc,
  b1_value, snapshot, delta_after_edit, delta_empty_token, table_sum, batch_applied,
  batch_d1, can_undo_before, undo, redo, persist_a1, register_udf, poll_events, panic,
  after_panic_lifecycle, err_dup_sheet, err_bad_kind, err_register_builtin, err_post_close),
  same recorded fields, same literal inputs (10, A1+1, F6=77, SUM(Sales[Qty]), C1*2,
  builtin 0). Neither stubs/skips a step. delta_after_edit pins schemaVersion + the
  changed-cell coordinate + value (not mere presence); poll_events pins sorted-unique kinds.
- **Output DTO key/camelCase parity.** snapshot (sheets/formats/dateSystem/version/
  schemaVersion), delta (changedCells/removedCells/sheetsChanged/sheetsRemoved/formatsAdded/
  version/fullRebuildRequired/fullRebuildReason/schemaVersion), batchResult (applied/version),
  undoRedo (consumed/version), cellSnapshot (row/col/value?/formula?/format?/rendered?),
  cellValue (kind+payload — both add `blank`: napi cell_value_json_from_session lib.rs:4453,
  pyo3 :372), eventPage (events/nextCursor/dropped), event (kind+per-variant: recalc_progress/
  cell_diagnostic/operation_completed/provenance/structure_changed/full_resync_required) —
  key-for-key identical between lib.rs:4444-5253 and src/lib.rs:352-1307. Absent Option fields
  omitted on both. fullRebuildReason enum strings identical (no_prior_version/cache_cleared/
  stale_horizon/epoch_mismatch — napi full_rebuild_reason_str lib.rs:392-399 vs pyo3 :499-504).
  DateSystem strings identical (Excel1900/Excel1904). (u64 sub-field REPRESENTATION is the
  HIGH-1/HIGH-2 exception; KEY parity is clean.)
- **Lifecycle gating is the engine's, identical for both bindings.** Neither binding adds
  gating — both call `self.inner.lock().<method>()` directly, so gating is the unchanged
  engine's (ensure_ready in ql-exec/src/session.rs). The golden flow empirically pins it:
  can_undo_before succeeds pre-close on both rows; err_post_close (a cell() after close())
  throws invalid_state on both (matrix passes → codes match). canUndo/canRedo bound ungated
  on both (lib.rs:6822/6829, src/lib.rs:988/993) per §3.8.
- **Deferred §2c bulk methods never silently succeed** — see INFO-1; both honor No-Fallbacks
  (Node loud Capability with `.map(|_|())` on the unreachable Ok arm, Python absent).
- **`js_name="Session"` confirmed** on the owning struct (lib.rs:5554 `pub struct Session {
  inner: Arc<Mutex<CoreWorkbookSession>> }`), wrapping `ql_exec::WorkbookSession` (the sole
  EngineSession impl). The legacy `CollabSession` (lib.rs:1214) is a SEPARATE class with its
  own `collab_session_error_to_napi` mapper (the `[kind]`-prefix-only legacy path) — NOT
  reachable from WorkbookSession methods and NOT the 6.3 surface. The golden emitter
  `new Session()` instantiates the owning class.
- **macOS linkage** (quantbook-py/build.rs): `-undefined dynamic_lookup` emitted only on
  macOS via `cargo:rustc-cdylib-link-arg`, scoped to this cdylib; Linux needs no flag.
  Correct for the non-maturin raw-cdylib load. Cargo.toml re-enables pyo3 `macros` (dropped
  by the workspace default-features=false pin) — necessary; abi3-py310 + extension-module
  compose from the pin.
- **Send/Sync positive proof** present on both (napi assert_send<CoreWorkbookSession> +
  assert_send/sync<Session> near file end; pyo3 src/lib.rs:1323-1329) per audit Rule 4.
- **pyo3 E0119 caveat handled correctly** — the debug-only probe lives INSIDE the single
  `#[pymethods]` block with a per-method `#[cfg(debug_assertions)]` (src/lib.rs:1069); the
  comment notes a second `#[pymethods] impl` would conflict without `multiple-pymethods`.

---

## BOTTOM LINE
Ship the freeze AFTER resolving HIGH-1 and HIGH-2 — the u64-representation fork
(BigInt-string in Node vs JSON int in Python on customPeer / Event.op / nextCursor /
TransactionId / recalc op-ids). These are frozen-in DTO-shape divergences that a JSON
consumer's two parsers would disagree on, and the matrix does not exercise them (it
value-masks version/nextCursor and never reads `op` or a custom format). Fix-or-document
MED-1/MED-2/MED-3 and LOW-1 in the same pass (each cheap; each closes a real divergence or
a coverage gap that freezing makes permanent). Record INFO-1/INFO-2 as written decisions.
The tested golden-flow surface is genuinely parity-clean and the panic/error/No-Fallbacks/
lifecycle contract is sound — but a phase-FREEZE must not lock the u64 wire asymmetry
without an explicit, tested decision.

— ENGINE OPUS lane (complete read).
